`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`
- The `allowed-packages` entry already in the file (`com.sun.xml.ws.encoding.fastinfoset`) is itself strong evidence for what `rt-fi` is: "fi" = Fast Infoset, the ITU-T/ISO binary XML encoding Metro uses as a faster alternative to text SOAP — so the only real research question was *where it lives*, not *what it does*.
- For multi-module Maven projects like this one, sibling artifacts published from the same GitHub repo almost always share one `repository-url`; the per-artifact variation is in the Maven Central path (`rt-fi-$version$-sources.jar`) and the javadoc.io path, both of which just substitute the artifactId — that's why I could derive high-confidence values by pattern-matching `rt`/`jaxws-rt`/`servlet` instead of needing a fresh search.
